= The chain at a glance <app-chain>

Every numbered statement in the guide, in order. The arrow shows the earlier statements that each one rests on. Axioms (A) are basic facts. Definitions (D) fix terms. Hypotheses (H) are claims that the evidence supports and does not settle, each held at stated odds. Propositions (P) are conclusions, and one that rests on a hypothesis is only as sure as the hypothesis. Forecasts (F) are judgments about the future.

